{"version":1,"kind":"summary","errors":22,"warnings":0,"explanations":{"E0050":"# E0050: a type that cannot be inferred\n\n`None` takes the optional type its position expects. Where nothing says which type, Sisu cannot choose one.\n\n## Why\n\nEvery optional is an optional of some type: `None` of `i64?` and `None` of `Tree?` are different values. A `let` with no type has nothing to take it from.\n\nThe help of a `let` with `None` or `[]` writes the type from the first later use of the local that gives one. A use can be a call argument, a `return`, an assignment or a `push`. When no use gives a type, the help writes `...` in its place, as in `let x: ...? = None`.\n\nA call of a generic function, class or variant has the same problem when nothing fixes one of its type parameters. `first([])` gives `T` no type: the `[]` has none of its own, and a later use of the result does not count. Annotate the result, `let x: i64? = first([])`, or write the type arguments, `first<i64>([])`. A parameter that the result names only through an associated type, as `S` in `-> [S.Item]`, is not fixed by an annotation of the result: write the type arguments, `collect<Countdown>()`.\n\nAn alias whose body does not use a type parameter has the same problem. In `type F<T> = f64`, no value gives `T` a type, so the compiler cannot infer `T` at `F.pi`. Write the type argument, `F<i64>.pi`, or remove `T` from the alias, `type F = f64`. Sisu gives no warning for a type parameter that nothing uses.\n\n`Some(None)` has the same problem: `Some` holds a value of any type, and `None` has no type of its own. Annotate the optional, `let x: i64?? = Some(None)`.\n\n`Ok(1)` has the same problem: `Ok` holds the value, and nothing says the type of the error. Annotate the result, `let r: Result<i64, string> = Ok(1)`. `Err(\"bad\")` leaves the type of the value open in the same way.\n\n`x ?? None ?? 0` has the same problem, because `??` groups to the right. It is `x ?? (None ?? 0)`, and nothing gives that `None` a type. To remove two layers from an `i64??`, write `(x ?? None) ?? 0`.\n\n## Broken\n\n```sisu\nfn main() {\n    let x = None\n}\n```\n\n## Fixed\n\n```sisu\nfn main() {\n    let x: i64? = None\n    print(x ?? 0)\n}\n```\n"}}
